# Squeeze Mapping (Quick Run)

## (random `x`, `x*`)
```bash
python examples/viscoelasticity/squeeze_jacobian.py \
  --random-mantissa \
  --random-count 40 \
  --random-low -2000 \
  --random-high 2000
```
This writes the heatmaps to:
- `examples/viscoelasticity/squeeze_offdiag_by_pq.svg`
- `examples/viscoelasticity/squeeze_offdiag_by_state.svg`

## Other useful combinations
```bash
# (random `x`, `x*`) + reproducible samples
python examples/viscoelasticity/squeeze_jacobian.py --random-mantissa --random-count 40 --random-low -2000 --random-high 2000 --random-seed 42

# Add Violin plot over FD deltas (1..10)
python examples/viscoelasticity/squeeze_jacobian.py --random-mantissa --random-count 40 --random-low -2000 --random-high 2000 --fd-delta-violin

# Use contiguous range instead of random x/x*
python examples/viscoelasticity/squeeze_jacobian.py --min-mantissa -20 --max-mantissa 20

# Custom p and q lists + custom FD delta (I did not use these, by default p and q are from 2 to 30, and FD delta is 1)
python examples/viscoelasticity/squeeze_jacobian.py --p 2 4 8 16 --q 3 6 12 24 --fd-delta 2
```
